# Cursor AI Rules for str8n Project

## JSDoc Documentation Standards
- Use simple code block syntax (```) without language identifiers in JSDoc examples
- Keep JSDoc comments concise and focused on functionality
- Include @example blocks for complex functions/components
- Use @param and @returns tags consistently
- Document all exported functions, components, and types
- Include clear descriptions of what each function/component does

## Code Style Guidelines
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use React Native and Expo patterns
- Follow the existing project structure and naming conventions
- Use proper TypeScript types and interfaces
- Prefer const over let when possible

## Project-Specific Rules
- This is a React Native/Expo project with Skia integration
- Use the existing context and store patterns
- Follow the established component hierarchy (atoms -> molecules -> organisms -> pages)
- Use the existing utility functions and services
- Maintain consistency with the current theme and styling approach

## File Organization
- Keep components in their appropriate directories (atoms, molecules, organisms, pages)
- Use index.ts files for clean exports
- Group related functionality together
- Follow the existing import/export patterns

## Performance Considerations
- Use React.memo for expensive components when appropriate
- Optimize re-renders with proper dependency arrays
- Use useMemo and useCallback for expensive computations
- Consider bundle size when adding dependencies 